# w2 — the wrap trick (mirrors demos/11-noita/w2-wrap.bqn)
# Wand [SB, DP], cast pointer at slot 1: the second block wraps — DP at the buffer's end binds the bolt at the front.
# rot is the block's draw order as world rows (DP first, then the wrapped SB), the deck rotation the host's cast pointer supplies.
n 3
col keys num 0 1 2
col wand bool 1 0 0
col spell bool 0 1 1
col slot num -1 0 1
col proj bool 0 1 0
col mod bool 0 0 1
col drawAdd num 0 0 1
col drawPos num 0 0 0
col bal num 0 0 0
col damage num 0 3 0
bind rot vec 2 1
